{{!-- The use pips ARE the control: a filled pip spends one use, an empty one restores one.
      There is no −/+ beside the other controls — two controls for one number was one too
      many. They sit inside the name span whose own action opens the item; a click lands on
      the innermost `data-action` and nowhere else, which is how core dispatches, so a pip is
      a pip and the name around it is still the name. One partial for both actor rows, so
      they cannot drift. On a sheet the user may not write, the pips are the count and nothing
      else: the glyphs without the anchors.

      @param uses      [filled, …] one per use
      @param editable  @root.editable — whether a pip spends and restores --}}
<span class="cairn-item-uses">
    {{#each uses as |filled|}}
    {{#if ../editable}}
    {{#if filled}}
    <a data-action="itemUseDecrement" data-tooltip="{{localize 'CAIRN.ItemSpendUse'}}"><i class="fa-solid fa-circle"></i></a>
    {{else}}
    <a data-action="itemUseIncrement" data-tooltip="{{localize 'CAIRN.ItemRestoreUse'}}"><i class="fa-regular fa-circle"></i></a>
    {{/if}}
    {{else}}
    <i class="{{#if filled}}fa-solid{{else}}fa-regular{{/if}} fa-circle"></i>
    {{/if}}
    {{/each}}
</span>
